      <h1>What Is the Bitcoin Halving?</h1>
      <p class="msc-learn-page__deck">The Bitcoin halving is a scheduled reduction in the block subsidy permitted by the consensus rules. It happens at defined block-height intervals, reduces the rate of new bitcoin issuance, and does not guarantee a particular price, miner response, or calendar date.</p>
      <ul class="msc-learn-page-meta"><li>Essentials</li><li>Surface</li><li>Explainer</li><li>9 to 11 minutes</li><li>Reviewed 2026-07-17</li></ul>
      <p class="msc-learn-preview-note">Preview only. Publication records and confirmed URLs do not exist; all navigation remains inactive.</p>
