    <section class="msc-learn-key-terms" aria-labelledby="MscGuide015Terms"><h2 id="MscGuide015Terms">Key Terms</h2><dl><div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Halving</dt><dd>The scheduled reduction in Bitcoin&#39;s block subsidy after each 210,000-block interval.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Block subsidy</dt><dd>New bitcoin created under the issuance schedule and paid through a block&#39;s coinbase transaction.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Transaction fee</dt><dd>The input value not reassigned to transaction outputs and available to the block&#39;s miner.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Miner</dt><dd>An operator that constructs candidate blocks and performs proof of work.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Mining</dt><dd>The proof-of-work process that orders valid transactions into blocks and competes to extend the Bitcoin chain.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Difficulty adjustment</dt><dd>Bitcoin&#39;s periodic recalculation of mining difficulty based on prior block timing.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Hashrate</dt><dd>An estimate of the total proof-of-work computation being applied to Bitcoin mining.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Consensus</dt><dd>The shared validation rules independently enforced by Bitcoin nodes.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Satoshi</dt><dd>The smallest standard unit of bitcoin, equal to one hundred millionth of one bitcoin.</dd></div></dl></section>
